This extension adds Borderlands 3 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]OpenHotfixLoader and Python SDK installed automatically.[/summary]

[b][size=3]This extension will automatically download and install the [url=https://github.com/apple1417/OpenHotfixLoader]OpenHotfixLoader[/url]﻿ and [url=https://github.com/bl-sdk/oak-mod-manager]Python SDK[/url]. These are required for many BL3 mods.[/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]OpenHotfixLoader mods with an "openhotfixloader.dll" file and a "b3hm.exe" file install to the "OakGame\Binaries\Win64\Plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Python SDK mods with a "unrealsdk.dll" file and a "sdk_mods" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]SDK mods with a ".py" file and a ".sdkmod" file install to the "sdk_mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Plugin Loader installs to the "OakGame\Binaries\Win64" folder, recognised by a "d3d11.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Hotfix mods with a ".bl3hotfix" file install to the "OakGame\Binaries\Win64\Plugins\ohl-mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with an "OakGame" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Pak mods with a ".pak" file install to the "OakGame\Content\Paks" folder.[/*]
[*]Movies mods with a ".mp4" file install to the "OakGame\Content\Movies" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods install to the "OakGame\Binaries\Win64" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Downloads and installs OpenHotfixLoader automatically from GitHub to "OakGame/Binaries/Win64/Plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs Hotfix mods (.bl3hotfix) to "OakGame/Binaries/Win64/Plugins/ohl-mods" folder. [b][color=#ffff00]Hotfixes are loaded automatically, no commands or web UI required![/color][/b][/*]
[*]Downloads and installs the Python SDK automatically from GitHub to "OakGame/Binaries/Win64" folder (also enables plugin loading).[/*]
[*]If your mod needs to be next to the game executable file (reshades, game .dll files, etc.), use mod type "Binaries (Engine Injector)".[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Borderlands 3 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Openhotfixloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "openhotfixloader.dll" file and a "b3hm.exe" file.

  Installs to: "OakGame\Binaries\Win64\Plugins"

========================================================================

Sdk:

Recognised when the archive contains a "unrealsdk.dll" file and a "sdk_mods" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Sdkmod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".py" file and a ".sdkmod" file.

  Installs to: "sdk_mods"

========================================================================

Pluginloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "d3d11.dll" file.

  Installs to: "OakGame\Binaries\Win64"

========================================================================

Hotfix:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".bl3hotfix" file.

  Installs to: "OakGame\Binaries\Win64\Plugins\ohl-mods"

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── OakGame\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "OakGame" or "Engine" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Pak:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".pak" file.

  Installs to: "OakGame\Content\Paks"

========================================================================

Movies:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".mp4" file.

  Installs to: "OakGame\Content\Movies"

========================================================================

Binaries:

Handled by the "testBinaries" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

  Installs to: "OakGame\Binaries\Win64"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

